  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "Rinse the baingan (eggplant or aubergine) in water. Pat dry with a kitchen napkin. Apply some oil all over and",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "d2255460-5a1e-5b9a-8a3d-3a97723651c7",
        "977c31ac-75be-50ab-9dfb-36cb00f53494"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "keep it for roasting on an open flame. You can also grill the baingan or roast in the oven. But then you won't get"
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "the smoky flavor of the baingan. Keep the eggplant turning after a 2 to 3 minutes on the flame, so that its evenly",
      "timer_seconds": 180
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "cooked. You could also embed some garlic cloves in the baingan and then roast it.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "109f7aaa-97ba-5977-af84-4a14cad328bd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 5,
      "instruction": "Roast the aubergine till its completely cooked and tender. With a knife check the doneness. The knife should slid",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "d2255460-5a1e-5b9a-8a3d-3a97723651c7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 6,
      "instruction": "easily in aubergines without any resistance. Remove the baingan and immerse in a bowl of water till it cools",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "d2255460-5a1e-5b9a-8a3d-3a97723651c7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 7,
      "instruction": "down."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 8,
      "instruction": "You can also do the dhungar technique of infusing charcoal smoky flavor in the baingan. This is an optional step."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 9,
      "instruction": "Use natural charcoal for this method. Heat a small piece of charcoal on flame till it becomes smoking hot and red."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 10,
      "instruction": "Make small cuts on the baingan with a knife. Place the red hot charcoal in the same plate where the roasted"
    },
    {
      "step_number": 11,
      "instruction": "aubergine is kept. Add a few drops of oil on the charcoal. The charcoal would begin to smoke.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "d2255460-5a1e-5b9a-8a3d-3a97723651c7",
        "977c31ac-75be-50ab-9dfb-36cb00f53494"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 12,
      "instruction": "As soon as smoke begins to release from the charcoal, cover the entire plate tightly with a large bowl. Allow the"
    },
    {
      "step_number": 13,
      "instruction": "charcoal smoke to get infused for 1 to 2 minutes. The more you do, the more smoky the baingan bharta will",
      "timer_seconds": 120
    },
    {
      "step_number": 14,
      "instruction": "become. I just keep for a minute. Alternatively, you can also do this dhungar method once the baingan bharta is"
    },
    {
      "step_number": 15,
      "instruction": "cooked, just like the way we do for Dal Tadka."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 16,
      "instruction": "Peel the skin from the roasted and smoked eggplant."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 17,
      "instruction": "Chop the cooked eggplant finely or you can even mash it."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 18,
      "instruction": "In a kadai or pan, heat oil. Then add finely chopped onions and garlic.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "c61ffb96-79c4-53da-b8ab-a0c490035830",
        "109f7aaa-97ba-5977-af84-4a14cad328bd",
        "977c31ac-75be-50ab-9dfb-36cb00f53494"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 19,
      "instruction": "Saute the onions till translucent. Don't brown them.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "c61ffb96-79c4-53da-b8ab-a0c490035830"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 20,
      "instruction": "Add chopped green chilies and saute for a minute."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 21,
      "instruction": "Add the chopped tomatoes and mix it well.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "4bd97609-bba3-5fad-ae72-b98633f1b817"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 22,
      "instruction": "Bhuno (saute) the tomatoes till the oil starts separating from the mixture.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "4bd97609-bba3-5fad-ae72-b98633f1b817",
        "977c31ac-75be-50ab-9dfb-36cb00f53494"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 23,
      "instruction": "Now add the red chili powder. Stir and mix well."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 24,
      "instruction": "Add the chopped cooked baingan."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 25,
      "instruction": "Stir and mix the chopped baingan very well with the onion­tomato masala mixture.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "c61ffb96-79c4-53da-b8ab-a0c490035830"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 26,
      "instruction": "Season with salt. Stir and saute for some more 4 to 5 minutes more.",
      "timer_seconds": 300,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "d144df40-4fe9-52d7-845c-3fe3a16b9411"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 27,
      "instruction": "Finally stir in the coriander leaves with the baingan bharta or garnish it with them. Serve Baingan Bharta with",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "a77c0c34-5ecb-5a3b-ae1a-e2cae5a8560a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 28,
      "instruction": "phulkas, rotis or chapatis. It goes well even with bread, toasted or grilled bread and plain rice or jeera rice."
    }
  ],
